# Build and tooling
node_modules
dist
.vite
coverage
*.log
.DS_Store

# Secrets. Nothing here should ever exist in this repo, and the day one does,
# it must not be one `git add -A` away from being published forever.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*.local

# Working notes, and anything written by or for an agent that is not a manual.
# AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, PLAN.md and the README files are the manuals and are
# tracked. Everything else of that shape is thinking, not product: session
# records, audits, transcripts, scratch analysis, private lists. Thinking is
# often about people, prices and plans, and it is not for publication.
#
# internal/ holds the design specimens and the shelved wallet mechanism. They
# are binding on whoever builds a screen, and they are not published. They then
# live only on the machine that has them: keep a backup outside git.
private/
internal/
notes/
*.private.md
*.notes.md
SESSION-*.md
AUDIT-*.md
TRANSCRIPT-*.md
scratch/

# Agent tool state. Shared config under .claude/ is tracked on purpose;
# per-machine and credential-bearing files are not.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
.grok/
.aider*
.cursorignore
# The manuals stay at the repository root so both agents auto-load them —
# neither reads them from a subdirectory — and are untracked so they are not
# published. Same for the deployment guides: they describe our own
# infrastructure. deploy/*.conf stays tracked, because src/csp.test.ts reads
# those two files to catch the deployed policy drifting from the app's.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/PLAN.md
deploy/README.md
deploy/chronik-agora.md
